			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/MountainClient): Enhance Mountain gRPC client with comprehensive fault tolerance and observability\n\nThis commit significantly upgrades the Mountain Client Service within the Cocoon extension host sidecar, transforming it into a robust, production-ready gRPC client with advanced circuit breaking, connection monitoring, and VS Code extension compatibility. Key enhancements provide the reliability required for persistent WebView panel state synchronization and session restoration.\n\n**Core Architectural Improvements:**\n- **Detailed Connection State Tracking**: Introduced `ConnectionState` enum (`DISCONNECTED`, `CONNECTING`, `CONNECTED`, `DEGRADED`, `FAILED`) replacing the simple boolean `isConnected`, enabling better lifecycle management.\n- **Enhanced Circuit Breaker**: Upgraded to track consecutive successes/failures with configurable thresholds, transition logging, and detailed state management (`Open`, `HalfOpen`, `Closed`) for fault isolation.\n- **Comprehensive Performance Metrics**: Added tracking for total requests, successes, failures, response times (average, min, max), and active request monitoring via a `Map<bigint, requestInfo>`.\n- **Graceful Shutdown**: Registered handlers for `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` signals and VS Code extension context detection for proper cleanup.\n- **Cancellation Support**: Integrated `CancellationToken` interface for VS Code extension API compatibility and request lifecycle control.\n\n**Operational Robustness:**\n- **Advanced Configuration**: Enhanced environment variable parsing with validation for host patterns (IPv4, IPv6, domains, Unix sockets), port ranges, retry limits, and health check periods.\n- **Connection Health Monitoring**: Proactive health checks with failure tracking, error persistence (`lastHealthCheckError`), and auto-reconnection logic with exponential backoff.\n- **Request Lifecycle**: Each request now generates a UUID, is tracked in `activeRequests`, and includes cancellation checks before execution.\n- **Error Classification**: Refined `isConnectionError` method to detect various gRPC, network, and system errors for appropriate recovery strategies.\n\n**Protocol & Communication:**\n- **gRPC Channel Configuration**: Specified optimized channel options (`keepalive_time_ms`, `max_receive_message_length`) for high-performance IPC.\n- **Improved Protocol Loading**: Enhanced `loadProtocolDefinition` with better fallback strategies and detailed error context when loading `Vine.proto`.\n- **Structured Error Handling**: RPC errors from Mountain are now parsed into structured JavaScript `Error` objects with `code` and `data` properties.\n\nThis upgrade establishes the Mountain Client Service as a foundational, resilient communication layer, directly supporting the reliable state persistence required by the WebView panel system and other Cocoon ↔ Mountain IPC flows.",
			"SHA": "34dac09fd197a41b11cb5fb9018ba5bf651f6d96"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
